1o5i|a|Prior; earlier; former. ; Earlier; sooner; before. ; More readily or willingly; preferably. ; On the other hand; to the contrary of what was said or suggested; instead. ; Of two alternatives conceived of, this by preference to, or as more likely than, the other; somewhat. ; More properly; more correctly speaking. ; In some degree; somewhat; as, the day is rather warm; the house is rather damp.	e:x5,8,3~x5,8,3
